{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"## The Fundamental Theorem of Calculus\n\nIf $~\\displaystyle g(x)=\\int_a^xf(t)\\,dt\\,$, then $~g^\\prime (x)=f(x)\\,$\n\nThis only works if $f$ is continuous on $[a,b]$.\n\nThankfully, the function $f(t) = t - t^2$ is continuous on $[-7,10]$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"## Applying the theorem\n\nWe're given:\n\n$\\displaystyle g(x) = \\int_{-7}^{x}(t - t^2)\\,dt\\,$\n\nSo the theorem tells us:\n\n$ \\displaystyle g\\,^\\prime(x) =x - x^2 $","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"## Evaluating $g'(10)$\n\n$\\displaystyle g'(10)= 10 - 10^2 = -90$\n\nThe answer:\n\n$g'(10)=-90$\n","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$\\displaystyle g(x) = \\int_{-7}^{x}(t - t^2)\\,dt\\,$\n\n$\\displaystyle g\\,'(10)\\, =$ [[☃ numeric-input 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"numeric-input 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answers":[{"maxError":null,"message":"","simplify":"required","status":"correct","strict":false,"value":-90}],"coefficient":false,"labelText":"","multipleNumberInput":false,"rightAlign":false,"size":"normal","static":false},"static":false,"type":"numeric-input","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}}}
